  "notes": "West leads the ♠Q against 3NT. South has only 7 top tricks (2 spades and 5 clubs). If South tries to develop tricks in diamonds, the defenders will be able to establish and run the spades before South can enjoy North's long diamonds.\n\nAfter winning the spade opening lead South should look towards hearts for the 2 extra tricks he needs. Playing to the ♥Q is almost certain to produce only 1 extra trick. If South plays a heart to dummy's ♥10, however, he will take 2 heart tricks whenever the ♥J is held by West.\n\nNotice that South cannot finesse against the ♥J in East's hand. If South crosses in clubs to play the ♥10 from North, if East has the ♥J, he will cover, holding South to 1 heart trick.",
